From 05840e0eb98664ee1cf5cfdb439da663a1cfa7b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:22:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FPU F4: integration gates -- receipts pair x2, x87 file
 byte-stability

The F4 row of docs/plans/FPU_PLAN.md, in the plan's measure-first style.

The --kernel= freestanding x87 payload (tests/fpu_payload.c) boots
through the loader core the CLI --kernel= flag drives and prints eight
COM1 receipts: FNINIT-anchored FSW bits, FLD1/FLDPI/FSIN(0.5)/FADD byte
pins (host-silicon payload) and the FBSTP/FBLD packed-BCD round trip.
tests/test_fpu_gate.c boots it twice on fresh machines and requires the
receipts byte-identical AND equal the pinned content (determinism x2);
t4_snapshot_lanes.sh runs the file through the real CLI split lane and
pins the receipt lines in the machine log.

Snapshot byte-stability of the x87 file -- measured defect: a computed
long double (FBLD's accumulator) assigned to an fst slot carried
run/ENV-dependent stack garbage into the slot's 6 padding bytes, and
the snapshot's raw cpu_t dump (machine.lo/machine.hi) wrote them into
the file -- two processes saving the same state produced different
snapshot files (flaky standalone, red under make's environment; two
bytes inside fst[7]'s padding). The fix is x87_w in src/cpu.c: every
one of the 24 fst write sites zeroes the slot padding, keeping the raw
dump byte-stable. The guest formats never leaked (FNSAVE emits 10
bytes/register, FXSAVE 10+zeroed reserved). Vectors: the gate's
fresh-run byte-identity and save->load->save fixed point, plus the t4
lanes (two-process file identity and the --max-instr=0 round trip --
a resumed halted run advances the device cadence by design, and a
resave must pass the same --kernel= or the machine-shape check refuses).

NC: engine reverted to F2 -> the payload dies "#UD x87 transcendental
out of scope (F3)", the gate red; run-dependent bytes injected at the
fst dump -> both lanes red at the first padding byte.

Gates: make test rc=0 (test-fpu 44 groups; test-table 369/369; t4 13
split lanes incl. the four F4 lanes), make test-sanitize rc=0,
diff-fuzz 512/12288 all-match, both SeaBIOS ISO lanes green.

docs/plans/FPU_PLAN.md (status + section 1e), docs/STATUS.md and
CHANGELOG.md updated in this commit; the plan F0-F4 is closed.
